  "stem": "Which of the following equations represents the same line as \\(y - 4 = -2(x + 1)\\) in the \\(xy\\)-plane?",
  "figure": null,
  "answer_type": "mcq",
  "choices": {
    "A": "\\(2x + y = 2\\)",
    "B": "\\(2x + y = 6\\)",
    "C": "\\(-2x + y = 2\\)",
    "D": "\\(2x + y = -2\\)"
  },
  "answer": "A",
  "spr_answers": null,
  "solution": [
    "Expand: \\(y - 4 = -2x - 2\\).",
    "Add 4: \\(y = -2x + 2\\).",
    "Add \\(2x\\) to both sides: \\(2x + y = 2\\)."
  ],
  "explanation": {
    "A": "Correct. \\(y - 4 = -2x - 2\\) gives \\(y = -2x + 2\\), or \\(2x + y = 2\\).",
    "B": "Incorrect. \\(-2(x + 1) = -2x - 2\\), not \\(-2x + 2\\).",
    "C": "Incorrect. This line has slope \\(2\\); the given line has slope \\(-2\\).",
    "D": "Incorrect. Adding 4 to \\(-2x - 2\\) gives \\(-2x + 2\\), not \\(-2x - 6\\)."
  },
